    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0469" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v10/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">888.2553/8–1452: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 200<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in the United
                            Kingdom</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d200-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-08-14T17:32:00-04:00">August 14, 1952—5:32
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1068. Fol <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> today handed to Burrows Brit Counselor: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Instrs to Middleton re proposed
                            reply to Mosadeq have been
                            carefully studied in Dept.</p>
                        <p>It is view of Dept that suggestion of informal conversations between Reps
                            of IranGov and of AIOC has merit and we
                            wld be pleased if Dr. Mosadeq
                            accepted this proposal.</p>
                        <p>Dept considers that alternate proposal, to be followed shld Dr. Mosadeq refuse suggestion for informal
                            conversations, wld be unacceptable to IranGov and wld leave gen
                            atmosphere worse rather than better. Reasons for this belief were set
                            forth in Secy’s msg to Eden of Aug
                            12 and need no elaboration here.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Bruce</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d200-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d200-f1-content">
                <p>Also sent to Tehran. Drafted and signed by Richards.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
